          "final_text_tail": "opagate as before; when there's no timeout, behavior is unchanged.\n  - Updated docstrings; kept `import threading` at the top level (permitted by the light-imports test) while doing lazy import of `logging` (not on the allowed list).\n- `src/click/shell_completion.py`: existing working-tree changes wrap context creation in `_resolve_context` with `with` blocks, so cleanup actually runs during completion \u2014 and now respects the timeout (propagated via `ctx_args`/`context_settings` and parent inheritance).\n\n558 tests pass, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed. The only failure in the full suite is a pre-existing pytest 9 collection incompatibility in `tests/test_basic.py` (verified to exist on a clean tree via `git stash`).\n\nImplementation summary:\n- `Context.__init__` accepts `cleanup_timeout` (default `None`), validates that it's a positive non-bool int/float (raising `ValueError` otherwise), stores it as `Context.cleanup_timeout`, and inherits it from the parent context.\n- `Context.close()` runs the exit stack on a daemon thread when a timeout is set, abandons it with a `logging` warning if it exceeds `cleanup_timeout`, and propagates cleanup errors if they complete in time. No behavior change for `None`.\n- The shell completion `_resolve_context` (working tree changes preserved) enters each resolved context via `with`, so completion cleanup now runs \u2014 and respects \u2014 the timeout.\n- Verified: 558 tests pass; `test_basic.py` has a pre-existing pytest 9 collection error unrelated to this change.",
